{
  "name": "Receive & route webhooks in self-hosted n8n (no public IP) — Webhook Relay",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📥 Receive & route webhooks in self-hosted n8n — no public IP\n\n**Who's it for**\nAnyone running n8n on localhost, a NAS, or behind a firewall/NAT who needs to receive webhooks (Stripe, GitHub, Shopify, your own apps) **without exposing n8n to the internet** — no tunnel, no port-forwarding, no reverse proxy.\n\n**What it does**\n[Webhook Relay](https://webhookrelay.com) gives your provider a stable public URL, authenticates the sender and answers it for you, then streams each event to n8n over an **outbound WebSocket** that n8n opens itself. n8n never listens for inbound connections.\n\n**How it works**\n1. **Webhook Relay Trigger** receives the event over the socket.\n2. **Normalize event** maps it to a small, consistent shape.\n3. **Route by event type** sends each type down its own branch.\n4. **Forward** POSTs to your endpoint (a Slack/Discord incoming webhook or any API); unmatched events are ignored.\n\n**Setup (2 min)**\n1. Install the community node: **Settings → Community Nodes → Install** → `n8n-nodes-webhookrelay`.\n2. Add a **Webhook Relay API** credential — API key from [my.webhookrelay.com/tokens](https://my.webhookrelay.com/tokens).\n3. Open the trigger's **Public URL** field to load the URL, and give it to your provider.\n4. **Activate** the workflow.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "aa000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -160,
        64
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1 · Receive — no public IP\nEvents arrive over an outbound WebSocket. Open **Public URL** on this node to get the URL for your provider.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "aa000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Section: receive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        544,
        272
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2 · Normalize & route\n**Normalize event** flattens the payload to a tidy shape. **Route by event type** then sends each type to its own branch.\n\n✏️ Replace the example event names (`created` / `deleted`) with your provider's own (e.g. GitHub `push`, Stripe `payment_intent.succeeded`).",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "aa000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Section: route",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        880,
        272
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3 · Act — edit these\n✏️ Point each **HTTP Request** at your own endpoint (a Slack/Discord incoming webhook, or any API). The **Other events** branch is dropped with a No-Op — replace it with your own handling.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "aa000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Section: act",
